 "finding": "December is forecast at 19.49 km2 (8 in 10: 13.1-25.7) vs a typical 22.25 km2: below normal, but inside the band.",
 "sections": {
  "what": "NISAR measured the lake on 11 passes from 2026-06-20 to 2026-10-30, including the 24 Sep day the camera saw only cloud. The summer drop is the normal irrigation cycle; the question is whether this year is unusual.",
  "why": "The reservoir feeds the Fergana valley's fields; how much water is left for winter and spring decides the first irrigation releases.",
  "radar": "Calm water is a mirror: it sends the L-band pulse away, so it looks dark in HH. A learned model on 10 radar features maps water at 40 m on every pass.",
  "validation": "On 8 photo days it never saw, the map matches Sentinel-2 at IoU 0.796 (95 % CI 0.745-0.853); shuffled labels score 0.067. ICESat-2 laser levels track the area (rho 0.946, n = 9).",
  "limits": "Wet mud on the drying shore reads as water (+2.56 km2 in late summer). The typical December rests on only 3 clear years. The model fails at other places so far.",
